{"kind":"request","text":"Claude: carry case C of #20008 through an explicit decision and, if adopted, complete delivery. This child preserves the remaining new-reader previous-snapshot outcome while the parent delivers shared head notices and safe qualification for an already-open browser. It is not satisfied by filing or landing a design alone.\n\nReconcile assessment #20194 and proposal #20195 against then-current main. A first-time reader during a rebuild currently has progress but no retained status. The resident may retain a previously verified same-profile snapshot, but serving it needs an explicit read contract and immutable ownership. Keep that remaining opportunity assigned here; do not call it already delivered or impossible solely because current /v0/status cannot serve it.\n\nPrepare the smallest source-backed design for ordinary adoption by Gitseq's ratifier before implementing any new read semantics. Reuse the existing proposal if its exact terms survive independent review, or publish a clearly linked replacement. Explain the first-time browser experience, selected frontier and interpretation identity, immutable publication/copy ownership, invalidation and failure behavior, bounded cost, and which clients consume the surface. Existing [status and rebuild handlers](internal/service/server.go@dfbf4089e6826810083848e56e9deff6c0faec29:479), [snapshot ownership](internal/app/app.go@dfbf4089e6826810083848e56e9deff6c0faec29:2490) and [browser state](ui/src/lib/store.ts@dfbf4089e6826810083848e56e9deff6c0faec29:30) are the starting evidence, not a frozen implementation specification.\n\nIn particular, do not infer that an ancestor check proves the descendant history is verified, or that the old in-memory projection is immutable merely because its struct header was copied. Specify whether an unverifiable current tail permits explicitly historical display or requires refusal, and obtain adoption for that choice; do not claim proposal #20195's ancestry check alone enforces its stated refusal. Preserve the parent's prohibition on exposing profile-invalid projections. No prior cache after a restart means no fabricated previous answer. /v0/status, /v0/wait, CLI/MCP current-frontier checks and admission retain their current contracts; a historical surface must not acquire authority by being displayed.\n\nThis request authorizes design and controlled evidence now, but no new read behavior before ordinary adoption. After adoption, implement the adopted outcome on this same assigned commitment, with actual server/browser tests for a first-time reader, same-profile forward rebuild, invalid profile, rewind, verification failure, missing cache, publication ownership/races, cancellation and bounded polling. Include positive and omission controls and working exact-head source/evidence previews. If the ratifier explicitly declines the feature, record that decision and the honest progress-only experience in the final source note instead; silence or a pending proposal is not a decline.\n\nUse request/previous-frontier-readers. Publish the reviewable design candidate without merging this implementation request prematurely. One final approved source landing closes this child only after the adopted behavior is delivered, or an explicit ratifier decision declines it and the resulting guidance is complete. Obtain independent Architecture/Security/Simplification review of the exact final head and all companions, ratify approval, seal main with full succession, push source/workroom refs, verify CI and remove the owned worktree/branch. Do not introduce new workflow states or a second verifier. No live-service, telemetry, install, reset, forge, key or #8162 operation.\n\nQueue design reconciliation after #20008, #20112 and #20258, before docs-only #20009; an adoption wait must not stop the already-assigned independent queue. I remain the requester responsible for its disposition. The original parent's already-open-browser safety and all notifier evidence remain on its existing commitment; this child does not waive them. Confirm availability and keep this assigned request through ordinary inherited staleness.","body":{"branch":"request/previous-frontier-readers","conditions":"Resolve new-reader previous-snapshot case C through explicit ordinary adoption and complete implementation if adopted, or explicit ratifier decline plus final guidance; design-only landing cannot close the full outcome. Independent exact-head review, seal/push/CI/cleanup.","head":"dfbf4089e6826810083848e56e9deff6c0faec29","stale_bases":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:0b8a9ff517318daec88e265b848e08ea877e98fa, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:11101b88b41221232f055686fe6639112a889c49, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:add297623a7c5f1d22725d891def3bcfe13ab87a stale; retired bases: git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:001b2e3b06105d22946682cb90201bc66c1c6a26, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:07e8e48166ea90a1d864c829f36902817926f6e7, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:092bd6cbe60056cd85ba626ea22807c1e97cc376, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:0a6f748b48ce807b2efbe9f4c8c245dda4d90359 and 105 more","target_head":"dfbf4089e6826810083848e56e9deff6c0faec29","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8","to":"a5d35aa7e4799472a208663d7f024917442bd513929f9eccf450628ccf70095d"}}